      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don't believe in automation in terms of moderation or administration. I find there's way too many 'unique' cases where it will either be abused, or overbearing on its players. Why do people think this stuff should be automated? Next time you cough on VRChat, you could get kicked. Next time someone walks into your room and makes sex sounds, you could be kicked...next time you and your mates are chilling to some banging music through someone's stereo mix / line in (VRChat instrument players), they'll get kicked.\n\nAutomation is not the answer for authority. However, I do feel that it would be beneficial if your rank in VRChat had weight to it. The higher rank you are, the more your vote/s count to getting someone kicked for someone below you. Something like this;\n\n----------\n\n>5 users happily talking\n>White person joins, blaring Russian speed techno\n>white person initiates kick on Russian 'musician'\n>3 votes (3/6 votes, vote failed) (2 people enjoyed the music)\n\n>5 users happily talking\n>White user joins, blaring Russian speed techno\n>Purple user initiates kick on Russian 'musician'\n>3 votes (vote passed) (purple user's vote counted twice because they're higher rank)\n\n----------\n\n^^^^ that sort of thing ^^^^",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
