  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So, we've all had the issue with a dreadful excuse for a human-being playing music, sounds, screaming or blasting content to deafen people. It's truly disgusting behaviour and it's becoming more and more common.\n\nWould it not be possible for VRchat worlds to recognise automatically when a user is the source of a sound which exceeds a certain volume, db, density or composition and automatically kick that person?\n\nSeriously. There's a pretty obvious difference between the sound wave of normal speech, music and sounds vs a violent bass signal or screech design to blow up peoples headphones and eardrums.\n\nReally, VRchat devs need to start finding out ways of limiting the amount of damage the less desirable people on Vrchat can cause to other users.",
